        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 12,
        "titulo": "Telling the time",
        "explicacao": "To ask: «Который час?» or «Сколько времени?». To answer, «час» changes like «рубль»: 1 → «час»; 2, 3 and 4 → «часа»; 5 to 12 → «часов». For half hours, say «половина» + the NEXT hour in the genitive: 2:30 = «половина третьего» (literally \"half of the third\"). To say at what time something happens, use «в» + the hour: «в три часа», «в пять часов». «Один час» becomes simply «в час».",
        "comparacao": "in English we say \"half past two\", counting from the hour that has gone. Russian counts toward the hour that is coming: \"half of the third\". (British English \"half two\" works the same way as the Russian.)",
